WEBVTT

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:12.570
<b>I tried coming alone to our usual park.</b>

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.070
<b>It's a feeling I've never felt.</b>

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:21.660
<b>Like a child, frightened by the sound of the wind</b>

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.670
<b>I ran back along the path home.</b>

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.970
<b>The sky outside the window is too vast. Where are you now?</b>

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.130
<b>Please, may this reach you...</b>

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:44.690
<b>Dear Lord, if you ever grant wishes,</b>

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:50.110
<b>grant my wish right now, please!</b>

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:56.240
<b>I want to hear your voice, I miss you! I want to see you now!</b>

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.830
<b>Why must you already be looking toward tomorrow?</b>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:06.210
<b>Don't just brush it off, saying the time has slipped by.</b>

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.540
<b>Once more...</b>

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:14.550
<b>I love you, and yet it's been too late since long ago.</b>

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:19.140
<b>Even if I give up, it can't be like the past.</b>

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.350
<b>Don't just decide so simply there's no way, no choice.</b>

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.230
<b>Smile once more.</b>

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:41.540
Come on, everyone!

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.860
Hurry up, hurry up!

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.650
Hold up!

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.040
Ms. Collins, you musn't dash out like that!

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.350
Come on, Heroman! Come on in!

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.030
I guess it was for the best?

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.770
Yeah, why not?

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:26.450
Can't help it now that she's seen him.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:30.710
Yeah. It seems like she 
was a big Heroman fan.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.350
Yup.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:37.630
And I bet she'd be more useful than 
the Professor when the chips are down.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.980
When it comes to school...

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.730
Well, I suppose so...

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.500
Joey!

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.850
Come on, Joey, Psy!

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:50.350
Let's go for a swim together!

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.860
Sure, I'll be right there!

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:09.660
Well, we still have Will to deal with. 
Can't blame you for being concerned.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:17.490
But that is that, and this is this.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.990
The beach, swimsuits, Lina!

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:22.870
What else do you need, man?

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.350
You should have fun when 
it's time to have fun.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.020
Your body ain't gonna hold 
up otherwise, you know?

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.020
You sure it's okay?

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.810
Yes! You have permission to have fun!

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.710
That's an order!

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.410
Hey!

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.300
It feels good!

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.850
Hurry up, hurry up!

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.550
We've all come to a southern island.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:07.960
Mr. Hughes arranged for us all to go to 
this government owned, uninhabited island!

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:13.900
And, with no other people
on the island to worry about,

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.560
we're having a lot of fun here with Heroman.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:39.290
Honestly... I'm really enjoying myself.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.710
This stuff's good!

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:54.920
Yum!

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:24.540
But yeah, I'm surprised the 
government has an island like this.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:28.310
Honestly. They say the 
world's in a recession,

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:31.100
but I guess that only 
applies to certain places.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:34.930
If those funds could have been
used for my research instead...

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:38.840
But thanks to this, we're
finally able to have fun

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.190
without worry about anything.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.360
What, you're satisfied already?

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.860
But the fun...

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:51.190
...has only begun!

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:01.110
What are you planning on doing, Psy?

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:03.590
Not some freaky ceremony or something, right?

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:07.810
After the beach, swimsuits, and a 
barbecue, this comes next, right?

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:11.000
Just to clarify... What 
are you talking about?

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.720
Isn't it obvious?

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.970
Ghost stories, man! Ghost stories!

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:27.150
It's a story I heard from one of the 
NIA staff on the charter plane here.

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:32.310
Before the government bought this 
island, it wasn't uninhabited.

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:36.300
There were definitely people living here.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:43.100
The reason that those people 
vanished from this island,

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:45.860
is because of a legend long told here...

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.010
The curse of the demon!

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:55.360
They say that anyone who 
sets eyes on the demon,

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:58.820
will meet with death soon 
afterwards, no matter what.

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:01.020
And that's what began happening.

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:05.890
With the growing number of victims,

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:09.330
the inhabitants of the island 
were faced with two choices.

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:12.920
Get cursed and throw away their lives,

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:14.660
or abandon the island...

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.410
So that's why this island is...

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:20.470
Yeah. Everyone's gone.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:24.670
Except for the demon, that is!

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:35.660
Hey, come on Professor. 
The story's just started.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:37.760
Can't you even handle this?

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:41.270
I'm fine, obviously.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.170
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:45.490
I am a self-styled child of science!

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.940
Worry not about me, and continue.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.260
Professor, behind you! Behind you!

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:53.050
What?!

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:08.000
The demon always appears on 
hot, humid nights like tonight.

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:15.430
Calm down, would you?

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:20.040
It's the right humidity, but 
it only shows up on windy days.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.460
No need to be worried.

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.730
Um, Psy...

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:25.720
What is it?

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:30.400
When you say windy... You 
mean windy like it is, now?

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:37.120
Yeah... About like this, probably.

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:46.500
It'll be okay, Mr. Denton. This story 
is a work of fiction, after all.

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:50.300
R-R-R-R-R-Right...

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:54.390
Yeah. And it's not like the lights 
are turning on and off for no reason,

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:58.120
or we're hearing rumbling sounds 
from far away... So, no worries.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.960
The lights are turning on and off...

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:13.070
And there's a rumbling sound from far away...

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:16.560
W-W-W-W-W-W-What's this mean, Psy?

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.580
How should I know?

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:21.100
I just heard about it, is all...

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:22.880
How does the story continue?

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.580
What is the name of the demon?

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.460
That name of the demon is...

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:37.260
Shapeshifter...

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:41.780
Just as the name says, it 
can change its form at will.

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:45.770
And it shows itself as the thing the 
people it curses fear the most.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:49.280
In front of the most fearful 
person in the village,

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:52.270
from the darkness on the 
other side of the door...

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:15.880
Calm down, Mr. Denton!

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:18.520
W-W-What's happening?

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:21.280
There shouldn't be anyone on this island!

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:24.680
H-H-Heroman... A-A-A...

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.390
Calm down everyone.

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:37.240
I said, calm down!

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:41.760
There's something not right about this.

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:45.000
That's why everyone's scared!

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:48.700
No! I mean the story is too good to be true.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:51.460
What do you mean?

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:55.390
You said you heard this ghost story
from a person from the NIA, right?

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:58.150
Yeah, but...

00:10:58.150 --> 00:11:00.290
Then that must be it.

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.270
What must be it?

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:04.320
S-S-S-So-So-So...

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:07.370
We're being set up by 
that person from the NIA.

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:10.330
Candid camera, you know?

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:12.970
Candid camera?

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:15.470
Otherwise this story 
matches up way too close.

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:18.110
It's going exactly as Psy's story said.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:22.470
I bet when we open this door, 
they'll be all like "surprise!"

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:25.580
And Joey's friends will come rushing in.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:27.700
You're going to open it?

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:31.270
Y-Y-Y-Y-Y-You're going to open it?

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:32.930
It'll be fine!

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:35.630
Here. Surprise!

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:52.400
Run.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.810
Huh? What?

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:59.660
Everyone... Run for your lives!

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:14.730
Everyone... Run for your lives!

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.990
He's injured...

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:25.820
Be careful when you move him.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.620
Mr. Denton, get the first-aid kit.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:29.070
R-Right...

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:56.900
Where am I?

00:12:56.900 --> 00:13:00.880
Don't worry. This is the 
lodge. There's no danger.

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:03.670
No! It'll be here soon!

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:05.960
Stay still!

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:08.800
The others must have already evacuated.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:12.270
You're the only ones left on the island...

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.570
Don't push yourself.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:15.930
Push myself?

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:20.450
We have to get out of 
here. Everyone, right now!

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:22.230
We'll all be wiped out!

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:23.440
Wiped out?

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.880
What's that supposed to mean, buddy?

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.510
Please explain.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.490
We had... an accident...

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:35.190
An accident?

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:37.610
I can't say any more!

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:38.890
Anyway, right now we...

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:43.180
Wait. If you are also a scientist, 
you should explain the situation!

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.390
Tell us the truth.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:50.190
I understand.

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:54.090
But I'll do it on the 
way. Hurry and get ready!

00:13:56.970 --> 00:13:58.350
Fine with us.

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:03.230
Hurry everyone.

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:14.790
We're good.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:16.000
Up we go.

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:25.480
You're the one I've heard about?

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:26.130
Yes?

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:29.720
This guy is really strong, right?

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:32.640
Y-Yes, he is!

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:34.960
I see.

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:37.530
That better be true, or else...

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:39.380
Or else...

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.710
Okay, let's go.

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:50.110
That noise...

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.580
We're too late?

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:58.880
Move away from the door!

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:07.460
What the hell is this?

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:13.550
Heroman...

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:16.100
Attack!

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.770
Heroman!

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:29.390
Everyone!

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:30.470
Lina!

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:15.720
Where am I?

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:18.310
Where is everyone?

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:24.580
Heroman! Everyone!

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:35.360
Lina!

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:15.090
Lina!

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:25.600
Lina... Lina. Lina!

00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:34.610
Lina!

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:42.910
Everything's all right now, Lina.

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:57.580
Lina... Lina!

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:01.140
Lina!

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:46.520
Joey?

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:48.600
Y-You're okay?

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.360
I...

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:55.770
You saved me?

00:18:55.770 --> 00:18:56.790
Yeah.

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:26.900
What's the matter?

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:29.740
Oh, it's nothing...

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:32.880
Looks like I got saved by you again, Joey.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:34.310
No!

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:35.310
You didn't really...

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:37.440
Thanks.

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.120
Hey, Joey...

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:47.240
I wonder where everyone went?

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:56.200
Oh, it's nothing. I'll go look for them soon.

00:19:56.200 --> 00:19:57.290
You wait here, Lina.

00:19:57.290 --> 00:19:59.000
No, I'm okay.

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:01.300
Take me with you.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:03.530
But...

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:08.140
I want to be with you, Joey. So... okay?

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:13.910
Okay.

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:35.040
Let's go.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:35.980
Yeah...

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:54.120
I wonder what in the world happened?

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:58.090
I don't really know. We were 
suddenly attacked, and then...

00:20:58.630 --> 00:21:00.690
...everyone got split up.

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:05.490
But I think everyone should be fine.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:08.320
That scientist told us 
to head to the airfield,

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:10.690
so I bet that's what they're all doing.

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:13.750
I sure hope so.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:14.840
Yeah...

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:20.960
W-Who is it?

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.490
Is somebody there?

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:31.470
It's you... You were safe?

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:34.210
That voice...

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:35.500
It's me.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:40.120
I'm the one you saved earlier.

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:47.870
My name is Ravi, thanks.

00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:49.830
I'm Joseph Jones.

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:52.700
It's too bad...

00:21:54.190 --> 00:21:57.680
It looks like it's too early to relax!

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:04.720
Lina, stay back!

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:05.510
Right!

00:22:06.520 --> 00:22:08.640
We're through!

00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:32.400
<b>I want to get to know you better,</b>

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:35.490
<b>to go at each other with our true feelings.</b>

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:41.830
<b>Your tears and smile are both here.</b>

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:46.260
<b>No matter how hard it is, I won't be scared any more.</b>

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:49.320
<b>With both of us, we can go anywhere.</b>

00:22:49.320 --> 00:22:54.760
<b>Since you're the one who taught me that I'm not alone.</b>

00:22:54.760 --> 00:23:02.450
<b>Every time I mutter the words "I was born to meet you"</b>

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:07.490
<b>my unease disappears, and my heart burns stronger.</b>

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:14.440
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:19.300
<b>Carve out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:23.840
<b>I can't move away from here.</b>

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:28.060
<b>Because I live feeling the same heartbeat.</b>

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:30.280
<b>I want to protect you to the very last,</b>

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:32.680
<b>to protect the promise built up.</b>

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:40.080
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:45.810
<b>We are carving out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:51.210 --> 00:23:52.700
On the next Heroman:

00:23:53.480 --> 00:23:57.130
Heroman, I'll save you! Count on it!

00:23:57.130 --> 00:24:01.750
It's a biohazard where plants have been 
transformed into living, willful weapons.

00:24:02.330 --> 00:24:05.540
The party has been split 
up thanks to its attack.

00:24:06.450 --> 00:24:08.040
In order to set things in order,

00:24:08.040 --> 00:24:11.660
Joey and Heroman head toward 
the center of the island.

00:24:12.360 --> 00:24:15.980
Next time on Heroman #19: Survival!

00:24:15.980 --> 00:24:18.660
Heroman... Attack!
